div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "Sure, I'll add it. First I'll look at how Claude Code stores conversations, so I know where to read the last reply from:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "Before touching the page, I'll check that the extraction returns the right reply, which should be my last reply to you (the Arabic one that ends with «"
  span.rtl[rtl]
    "أضيفه؟"
  "»):"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "Now the templates: I'll pass the display mode to the page and add styles for headings, quotes, code blocks and dividers. In the HTML page:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "Now the commands themselves need to pass the option through to the script. I'll first check how PowerShell handles "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "--last"
  " when it's passed to the script:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "PowerShell swallows "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "--last"
  " and "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "-last"
  " without passing them on, because it treats them as parameter names. I'll test adding a "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "-Last"
  " switch:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "With a "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "-Last"
  " switch, both "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "--last"
  " and "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "-last"
  " work. Anything unknown ends up in "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "$args"
  ", so I'll show an error for it:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "The screenshots worked, but the file name came out wrong ("
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "\\\\$n"
  " stopped the variable from expanding). I'll fix the path:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md.en[ltr]
  "The page has no Arabic boxes inside the code block at all. Either the browser loaded an old copy of the page from cache, or "
  span.ltr.code[ltr]
    "fillEnglish"
  " wasn't called. I'll check the file itself:"
div.ln.md[rtl]
div.ln.md[rtl]
